# cuts/v1.0.39/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.39. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.39, by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh, by scripts/resolve_cut_daemon_pin.sh,
# and by OS003 bin/cut.sh load_cut().
#
# THIS FILE IS THE AUTHORITATIVE HALF. OS003 carries a second cuts/v1.0.39/
# cut.env holding the operator's LOCAL PATHS. They are deliberately different
# documents. Do not merge them: vendoring OS003's copy here was tried and
# reverted because it carried operator working record, private box IPs and
# notarisation submission IDs into this PUBLIC repo.
#
# WHY v1.0.39 EXISTS: v1.0.38 SHIPPED A PRODUCT THAT DOES NOT WORK
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The v1.0.38 DMG verified, installed and passed every gate. The product on it
# stops growing about an hour after install and cannot answer a question about
# the customer. Four merged fixes and one new daemon are sitting unshipped.
#
#   #939  com.ostler.fda-rerun exits 1 hourly (ModuleNotFoundError: nameparser)
#         on every shipped box. Install runs in a /tmp staging tree; the #805
#         fix installed ostler_fda THERE and proved the import THERE, and
#         promote then destroys that venv and rebuilds it from a list
#         ostler_fda was never on. fda-rerun is the ONLY recurring ingest for
#         contacts, calendar, iMessage, WhatsApp, browsing and notes, so the
#         graph freezes at install-time contents. Measured on the walked box:
#         the tick's own interpreter cannot import the module at all.
#   #940  /api/v1/preferences served count:0 over a Qdrant collection holding
#         9,879 points. Writer and reader disagreed on a path and BOTH
#         reported success; the emitter was vendored correctly and invoked by
#         nothing.
#   #942  the upgrade path never repaired that venv, so #939 reached NEW
#         INSTALLS ONLY and an already-installed box stayed frozen through
#         every future update (HR015 #595).
#   #943  the daemon fallback could never complete: one baked integrity pin,
#         not re-pointed on retry, so the rescue path checked the fallback
#         tarball against the primary's digest and aborted telling the
#         customer their download looked tampered with (HR015 #583).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DAEMON CHANGED. 0.4.60 -> 0.4.61, AND THE PIN IS DERIVED, NOT COPIED
#
# hub-v0.4.61 carries ostler-assistant #325: pwg_preferences had NEVER decoded
# a real reply (its untagged enum knew `preferences`; the endpoint sends
# `interests`), the domain filter returned nothing for EVERY domain because
# the endpoint is case-sensitive and the tool lower-cased the value, a phrase
# handed to a person tool fuzzy-matched to a component supplier, and
# pwg_overview is new.
#
# Read out of the artefacts, cross-checked, because a version/checksum pair
# came apart on v1.0.29 with no gate watching it:
#
#     git rev-parse hub-v0.4.61^{}          bda4d7d837a086dc5008decfb1a7b5aeac616d68
#     daemon  DAEMON_FRONTEND_COMMIT        bda4d7d837a086dc5008decfb1a7b5aeac616d68
#     wrapper WRAPPER_FRONTEND_COMMIT       bda4d7d837a086dc5008decfb1a7b5aeac616d68
#     Ostler.app OSTLER_HUB_BUILD_COMMIT    bda4d7d837a086dc5008decfb1a7b5aeac616d68
#     gui/Makefile  DAEMON_VERSION          0.4.61
#     install.sh    OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION 0.4.61
#     install.sh    DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256 ff7b0b63...ced24
#
# The two FRONTEND sentinels are the pair verify_commit_parity.sh actually
# compares, and both were read from the COMPILED binaries with `strings`, not
# from a build log. build-hub.sh prints a resource-file stamp and then warns
# in its own output that parity must not be inferred from that line.
#
# THE HUB APP HAD TO BE BUILT. hub-v0.4.61 was promoted with the DAEMON only,
# and gui/Makefile:278 derives HUB_APP_TARBALL_NAME from DAEMON_VERSION, so
# this cut would have died at download-hub-app. Built from bda4d7d8 and
# published to ostler-assistant hub-v0.4.61, with the stale-bundle control
# fired: an Ostler.app stamped 8ba3e948 (the 0.4.60 build) was on disk first
# and both its stamp and mtime moved.
# ============================================================================

CUT_VERSION=1.0.39

# The daemon. hub-v0.4.61, signed, notarised and stapled. CHANGED in this cut.
DAEMON_COMMIT=bda4d7d837a0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THE CM051 PIN BELOW IS PROVISIONAL UNTIL THIS CHANGE MERGES.
#
# It must name the tree whose install.sh ships, compared BY BLOB. This file is
# itself part of a change that edits install.sh, so the pin cannot be final
# until the merge commit exists. RE-POINT IT AFTER THE LAST MERGE AND BEFORE
# THE TAG, then confirm with:
#
#     bash scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh --ref origin/main
#
# v1.0.31 was burnt by a pin chosen early and trusted. Ancestry is not a
# defence: it proves ordering and says nothing about content.
#
# ⚠️ AND SEE HR015 #600 BEFORE YOU TOUCH THE v1.0.38 RECORD. That gate reports
# a SHIPPED cut's record stale forever, because it compares against HEAD and
# main is supposed to move on after a tag. Its remediation text says to
# re-point the pin, which post-ship falsifies the register. This warning is
# about v1.0.38's record, NOT this one: for a cut still being prepared,
# comparing against HEAD is exactly right.
CM051=90e8d613207df53b318bafc1e180554aa5e67802
